    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bradford, Iowa, was named after an early settler family and officially platted on November 19, 1906, by the Bradford Town Site Company, driven by railroad interests.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bradford_franklin_county_iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Franklin County, where Bradford sits, was created by Iowa in 1851 but stayed unorganized until 1855, during which it was attached to neighboring Hardin and Chickasaw counties.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bradford_franklin_county_iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bradford’s post office opened in 1907, marking the town’s first official federal presence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://roadsidethoughts.com/ia/bradford-xx-franklin-profile.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town sits at an elevation of 1,250 feet above sea level, giving it a modest hilltop feel.",
